# Verify before commit

Before running `git commit`, verify the workspaces that have changes. Do not commit if any step fails — fix it and re-run.

## Web (`apps/web`)

```bash
npm run lint
npx tsc --noEmit
npm run build
```

If `next dev` is running, stop it (or accept that `.next` is shared) before `npm run build`.
A stale `.next` can cause a false `PageNotFoundError`; clear it and rebuild:

```bash
Remove-Item -Recurse -Force .next -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue; npm run build
```

## API (`apps/api`)

```bash
npm run lint
npm run build
npm test
```

`apps/api` lint runs with `--fix`, so re-check `git status` afterwards and stage any files it rewrote.

## Rules

- Run the checks for every workspace touched by the change, not just one.
- Report the results in the summary before committing.
- Never use `--no-verify` or skip these checks to get a commit through.
